    a: "<b>Cholinesterase Inhibitors — Pharmacokinetics:</b><br><b>Donepezil (Aricept):</b><ul><li>Piperidine-based; highly selective for AChE</li><li>Half-life: <b>~70 hours</b> — once-daily dosing</li><li>Hepatic metabolism (CYP2D6, CYP3A4)</li><li>Available: 5 mg, 10 mg, 23 mg tablets; orally disintegrating</li><li>Approved: Mild, moderate, and severe AD</li></ul><b>Rivastigmine (Exelon):</b><ul><li>Carbamate; inhibits BOTH AChE and BuChE (butyrylcholinesterase)</li><li>Half-life: ~1–2 hours (but 24h transdermal patch available)</li><li>Hepatic metabolism bypassed with patch — better GI tolerance</li><li>Approved: Mild-moderate AD; mild-moderate PDD</li></ul><b>Galantamine (Razadyne):</b><ul><li>Phenanthrene; inhibits AChE + modulates nicotinic receptors</li><li>Half-life: ~7 hours</li><li>CYP2D6 and CYP3A4 metabolism</li><li>Approved: Mild-moderate AD</li></ul>"
